--- title Saying how much with a position
--- about /part takes a count or a series position. Given a position it
--- about means "as far as there", and the two positions may be in
--- about either order -- the span is between them, taken from whichever
--- about comes first.

--- id parts/taking-up-to-a-later-position
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
s: "123"
take/part s skip s 1
--- result
"1"

--- id parts/the-two-positions-may-be-the-other-way-round
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is why this is a span rather than a direction: the same
--- note two positions give the same answer either way.
--- code
s: "123"
take/part skip s 1 s
--- result
"1"

--- id parts/taking-up-to-two-along
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
s: "123"
take/part s skip s 2
--- result
"12"

--- id parts/a-span-that-starts-partway-in
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
s: "123"
take/part skip s 1 skip s 2
--- result
"2"

--- id parts/a-span-of-nothing
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The degenerate case: the same position twice takes nothing.
--- code
s: "123"
take/part s s
--- result
""

--- id parts/copying-up-to-a-position
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
s: "123"
copy/part s skip s 2
--- result
"12"

--- id parts/copying-with-the-positions-reversed
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
s: "123"
copy/part skip s 2 s
--- result
"12"

--- id parts/taking-a-span-from-a-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2 3]
mold take/part b skip b 2
--- result
"[1 2]"

--- id parts/copying-a-span-from-a-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
b: [1 2 3]
mold copy/part b skip b 2
--- result
"[1 2]"
